"_doc": "D-217 crossing corridors, candidate set r3 (2026-11-16), made by mk_corridors.py from the p2c routing (board frame, mm). Inside a corridor the RF line is 0.975 mm wide, the near plane stays solid (In1 under F.Cu rows, In4 under B.Cu columns) and logic on In2/In3 may cross. Outside the corridors In1 to In3 (rows) or In2 to In4 (columns) are cut 2.975 mm each side of the line centre and the router keeps In2/In3 out. Corridors the routes do not use are removed after routing. Entries with kind narrow: short pad-adjacent pieces where a 1.95 mm line would come closer than 2.0 mm to other copper; same treatment as a corridor (D-217 r2). r2: corridors sized 0.7 mm per crossing net + 2 x 1.25 mm, at most 5 nets per corridor (r1: 0.5 mm, 9 nets; the router did not converge, 18 to 24 failed connections per pass). r3: every corridor 6 mm (r2: 8 nets failed after 10 passes, +12V_SW, A1/A2_BIAS, D602-A among them). Pruned 2026-11-20 after routing r4 (D-218): corridors with no In2/In3 copper within 2.975 mm of the line removed (list in 'dropped'). Then each kept corridor trimmed to the copper in it plus 1.0 mm each side (at least 1.5 mm).",
